   plot="Old Martin Chuzzlewit, convinced that his relatives are waiting for his money, has taken in the orphan Mary Graham as a companion; his grandson Martin is disinherited for falling in love with her. Martin is articled to the architect Seth Pecksniff, whose hypocrisy and whose daughters Cherry and Merry drive the plot of self-interest, and he leaves for America with Mark Tapley, where the Eden land-scheme swindle and the comic Americans (Colonel Diver, Mrs Hominy, Hannibal Chollop) expose a fraudulent democracy. The novel's darker plot is the murder of Montague Tigg by Jonas Chuzzlewit, and the resolution restores the repentant Martin to his grandfather's favour.",
