   plot="Mr Dombey, of the shipping house Dombey and Son, despises his daughter Florence and invests all his pride in his son Paul, who dies at Dr Blimber's school. Dombey's second marriage, to the proud Edith Granger, collapses when she elopes with his manager Carker, who is killed by a train at the novel's climax; Dombey is ruined by Carker's speculations, and is restored only by Florence's return with her husband Walter Gay and her child.",
