   plot="In the cotton town of Coketown, Thomas Gradgrind educates his children Louisa and Tom on 'facts'; Louisa marries the manufacturer Josiah Bounderby, the self-made 'Humbug' of the novel, and nearly elopes with the political adventurer James Harthouse before returning to her father's house broken. Tom robs the bank and is exposed by the circus girl Sissy Jupe's circle; Stephen Blackpool, the hand-loom weaver, is falsely accused, refuses to join the union, and dies down a mine shaft; Rachael nurses him, and the circus, with its horse-riding and its 'fancy', stands against the school of fact.",
